Article 4 (Allowances, etc.)
(1) The daily remuneration and allowances of expert commissioners shall be determined by the Council of Supreme Court Justices within budgetary limits each year.
(2) Full-time expert commissioners and appraisal management commissioners shall be paid the following allowances: Provided, That allowances shall not be paid in duplicate where one person concurrently serves as both a full-time expert commissioner and an appraisal management commissioner. <Newly Inserted on November 1, 2016; amended on November 29, 2024.>
1. Meal allowance;
2. Transportation support allowance;
3. Materials investigation and research allowance;
4. Management duty allowance;
5. Full-time service allowance;
6. Case allowance.
(3) The presiding judge may increase the allowances referred to in paragraphs (1) and (2) 6 within budgetary limits, taking into account the complexity of the matter, the nature of the duties performed by the expert commissioner, the time required for participation in litigation proceedings, etc. <Amended on November 1, 2016.>
(4) Domestic travel expenses and accommodation charges of expert commissioners shall not exceed the amount prescribed for persons falling under item 2 of the Domestic Travel Expense Payment Table in attached Table 2 referred to in Articles 10 through 13 and Article 16 (1) of the Rules on Travel Expenses of Court Public Officials. <Amended on January 9, 2009; and November 1, 2016.>
(5) Where an expert commissioner travels abroad, travel expenses and accommodation charges shall not exceed the amounts specified in Articles 10 (2), 11 (2) and 13 (2) of the Rules on Travel Expenses of Court Public Officials; the amounts for "Other Persons" in the Fixed International Airfare Table in attached Table 3 referred to in Article 12 (2); and the amounts for persons falling under subparagraph 2 (a) of attached Table 1 in the Fixed Overseas Travel Expense Table in attached Table 4 referred to in Article 16 (1). <Amended on January 9, 2009; and November 1, 2016.>
(6) Allowances, daily remuneration, travel expenses and accommodation charges of expert commissioners shall be paid from the National Treasury and shall not be included in litigation costs. <Amended on November 1, 2016.>
